.TH TOUCH 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
touch \- change file access and modification times
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B touch
.RB [ \-acm ]
.RB [ \-r
.I ref_file
.RB | \-t
.IR time ]
.I file
.RI [ file ]\ .\|.\|.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B touch
updates the access and/or modification times of each
.I file
operand, to the current time unless
.B \-r
or
.B \-t
is given. Multiple operands are processed in turn; an error on one
operand does not stop the rest from being attempted.
.PP
If a
.I file
operand does not name an existing file, it is created (as an empty,
ordinary file with the platform's default permissions) unless
.B \-c
is given, in which case that operand is skipped entirely, with no
diagnostic and no effect on the exit status.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
Change the access time of
.IR file .
Do not change the modification time unless
.B \-m
is also given.
.TP
.B \-m
Change the modification time of
.IR file .
Do not change the access time unless
.B \-a
is also given.
.IP
If neither
.B \-a
nor
.B \-m
is given, or both are given, both times are changed.
.TP
.B \-c
Do not create a
.I file
operand that does not already exist, and do not write a diagnostic or
count it as a failure when this happens.
.TP
.BI \-r " ref_file"
Use
.IR ref_file 's
own access and modification times instead of the current time.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-t .
.TP
.BI \-t " time"
Use the explicit
.I time
instead of the current time, given as
\fI[[CC]YY]MMDDhhmm[.SS]\fR
\(em all-numeric fields, each exactly two digits except the optional
leading century/year prefix. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-r .
.RS
.TP
.I MM
Month, 01\-12.
.TP
.I DD
Day of month, 01\-31.
.I DD
is only range-checked against 01\-31; it is not validated against
the number of days in
.IR MM 's
month.
.TP
.I hh
Hour, 00\-23.
.TP
.I mm
Minute, 00\-59.
.TP
.I SS
Seconds, 00\-60, if the optional
.B .
.I SS
suffix is given; 00 otherwise.
.TP
.I YY
Year within century, if given without
.IR CC .
A
.I YY
of 69\-99 means 1900+\c
.IR YY ;
a
.I YY
of 00\-68 means 2000+\c
.IR YY .
.TP
.I CC
Century, if given. Combined with
.I YY
as
.RI ( CC " times 100) + " YY .
.PP
If neither
.I CC
nor
.I YY
is given (a bare
.IR MMDDhhmm ),
the current year is used.
.RE
.TP
.B \-d
Not implemented.
.B touch
prints a diagnostic and exits immediately with status 1 rather than
parse only part of the ISO\ 8601 date/time grammar this option is
conventionally given.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I file
A pathname of a file whose access and/or modification time is to be
changed (and, ordinarily, created if missing).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The utility executed successfully and all requested changes were made.
.TP
.B >0
An error occurred: an invalid option, a missing operand, a missing
.B \-r
or
.B \-t
argument, both
.B \-r
and
.B \-t
given together, an invalid
.B \-t
.IR time ,
or a failure creating or updating the times of one or more of the
named files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cp (1),
.BR ln (1)
